#!/bin/zsh
TMUX=/opt/homebrew/bin/tmux
[ -x "$TMUX" ] || TMUX=/usr/local/bin/tmux
send() {
  $TMUX send-keys -t $1 C-u; sleep 1
  $TMUX send-keys -t $1 "$2"; sleep 2
  $TMUX send-keys -t $1 Enter; sleep 2
  $TMUX send-keys -t $1 Enter; sleep 1
  echo "sent -> $1"
}
send ETA-Refuter:1.1 "CHANGE OF TASK - the queue refutation is on hold because scribe3 came back with no data access, so there is nothing yet to refute. REFUTE THIS INSTEAD, and it is the most consequential diff of the day. scribe built three fixes to the voice enrolment write path in a worktree named enrol-wt, on top of 45eedda. You did not build it. WHAT IT CLAIMS: one, lib/voice-samples.ts now uploads every clip BEFORE any row is written and refuses the session outright if audio cannot be retained - previously six of seven voiceprints kept no audio at all and could never be recomputed. Two, a new lib/audio-duration.ts measures each clip from the Matroska Segment Info Duration, falling back to the last Cluster Timecode, claimed to under-report rather than over-report and to return null when it cannot tell; duration_ms is now stored and floors of MIN_CLIP_MS 3000 and MIN_SESSION_MS 30000 are enforced where previously the ONLY gate was a count of three clips with no duration check anywhere in the repo. Three, samples plus centroid now write in one driver batch rather than insert-then-recompute. Reported gate: 10 new tests, 6 red before the fix, mutations retention 1 fails duration 3 fails atomicity 2 fails, full suite 145 files 3261 passed 1 skipped 0 failed, typecheck 0. WHAT I WANT ATTACKED, hardest first. A. The duration parser is the risky part - it is new code reading a binary container format by hand. Feed it a real MediaRecorder webm from the actual enrolment UI, not a synthetic one; a live MediaRecorder stream carries no Segment Info Duration element at all, which is precisely the case the fallback exists for. Prove the fallback is exercised and prove the under-report claim rather than accepting it. A parser that silently returns a wrong duration now gates enrolment. B. Refusing the session when audio cannot be retained turns a soft failure into a hard one - what happens to a clinician mid-enrolment if blob storage is briefly unavailable, and is that failure